& [CorrectionPrinciple] is identity, definition, and state separation
  + a stable key answers which continuing subject is referenced
  + an immutable revision answers which exact purpose, program, policy, or endpoint definition applies
  + an immutable snapshot answers what lifecycle and cursor state was accepted at one transition position
  + an ordered transition answers how one snapshot lawfully followed another
  = must: bind each record to its exact profile and content digest when later canonicalized
  - never: place a normally mutable field in a stable key

& [StableKeySet] contains only durable coordinates
  + [AgentKey] contains one nonzero agent_uuid
  + [EnvironmentKey] contains one nonzero environment_uuid
  + [EndpointKey] contains one EnvironmentKey and one nonzero endpoint_uuid
  + [SessionKey] contains one nonzero session_uuid
  + [ProviderJobKey] contains one disposable provider_job_uuid for attribution only
  = must: compare complete keys exactly
  = must: treat UUID uniqueness as a registration obligation rather than proof contained by the value
  - never: infer purpose, program, authority, availability, physical existence, lifecycle, or effect capability from a key

& [AgentDefinitionRevision] is immutable configured meaning for one AgentKey
  + [definition_revision_uuid] is immutable identity
  + [agent_key] is one AgentKey
  + [predecessor_definition_digest] is absent for the first revision or binds the prior complete revision
  + [purpose_contract_digest] identifies the admitted purpose and completion boundary
  + [program_set_digest] identifies the admitted Cantor program set
  + [maximum_authority_digest] identifies the ceiling available for later projection
  + [created_from] identifies commissioning or registration lineage
  + [definition_digest] binds the complete canonical revision content
  = must: create a new revision for every purpose, program, or maximum-authority change
  - never: mutate an accepted definition revision in place

& [AgentRuntimeSnapshot] is immutable accepted state for one AgentKey
  + [agent_snapshot_uuid] is immutable identity
  + [agent_key] is one AgentKey
  + [definition_digest] identifies one exact AgentDefinitionRevision
  + [predecessor_snapshot_digest] is absent for the first snapshot or identifies the prior accepted snapshot
  + [transition_sequence] is zero for the first snapshot and increases exactly by one
  + [lifecycle] is active, suspended, retired, or faulted
  + [semantic_state_cursor] is one immutable SemanticStateCursor
  + [episode_cursor] is optional immutable EpisodeCursor
  + [active_session_key] is absent or identifies one nonterminal SessionSnapshot lineage
  + [snapshot_digest] binds the complete canonical snapshot content
  = must: reject forks under one single-writer transition lineage unless a later branch policy is separately signed
  = must: reject any snapshot whose definition, predecessor, sequence, cursor, or active session does not resolve coherently

& [EnvironmentRevision] is immutable configured environment meaning
  + [environment_revision_uuid] is immutable identity
  + [environment_key] is one EnvironmentKey
  + [predecessor_environment_digest] is absent or binds the prior revision
  + [environment_profile] is one versioned provider-neutral contract
  + [adapter_profile_digest] binds the adapter contract version
  + [instance_descriptor_digest] binds the configured environment instance description
  + [authority_domain_digest] binds the environment policy domain
  + [environment_revision_digest] binds complete canonical content
  = must: create a new revision after any adapter, instance, profile, or policy change

& [EndpointRevision] is immutable configured endpoint meaning
  + [endpoint_revision_uuid] is immutable identity
  + [endpoint_key] is one EndpointKey
  + [environment_revision_digest] identifies the exact containing environment revision
  + [predecessor_endpoint_digest] is absent or binds the prior endpoint revision
  + [endpoint_generation] is a positive adapter-declared generation coordinate
  + [endpoint_kind] is a closed adapter-declared semantic kind
  + [adapter_locator_digest] is an opaque adapter-resolved locator
  + [sharing_policy] is exclusive, shared_read_only, or adapter_governed
  + [endpoint_revision_digest] binds complete canonical content
  = must: make reset or replacement a new endpoint revision even when EndpointKey remains stable
  - never: use endpoint generation or revision as proof of current availability or physical control

& [SessionSnapshot] is immutable accepted binding state for one SessionKey
  + [session_snapshot_uuid] is immutable identity
  + [session_key] is one SessionKey
  + [agent_key] is one AgentKey
  + [agent_definition_digest] binds one exact AgentDefinitionRevision
  + [environment_revision_digest] binds one exact EnvironmentRevision
  + [endpoint_revision_digest] binds one exact EndpointRevision
  + [authority_projection_digest] is no broader than agent maximum authority and environment policy
  + [purpose_projection_digest] is no broader than the agent purpose
  + [predecessor_session_key] is absent for first binding or identifies the prior terminal or suspended session being resumed or replaced
  + [predecessor_snapshot_digest] is absent for the first session snapshot or identifies the prior snapshot of this session
  + [transition_sequence] is zero for proposed and increases exactly by one inside the session
  + [lifecycle] is proposed, bound, suspended, released, expired, or faulted
  + [snapshot_digest] binds the complete canonical snapshot content
  = must: create a new SessionKey for every resume from another session
  = must: reject changed agent, environment, endpoint, purpose, authority, or predecessor coordinates within one SessionKey
  = must: reject lifecycle forks and every undeclared transition
  - never: treat a SessionSnapshot as adapter availability, exclusive ownership, or physical binding proof

& [ImmutableCursorCorrection] removes mutable disposition
  + [SemanticStateCursor] is state_uuid, fabric_digest, projection_digest, and transition_position only
  + [EpisodeCursor] is episode_uuid, last_committed_event_uuid, and episode_digest only
  + whether a cursor is selected, replaced, invalidated, or closed is represented by an AgentRuntimeSnapshot transition or later episode authority
  = must: keep cursor bytes immutable after construction
  - never: update a disposition field on a cursor in place

& [BindingClaimCorrection] references exact state rather than nesting it
  + [claim_uuid] is immutable identity
  + [agent_key] and [agent_snapshot_digest] identify the exact proposing agent state
  + [environment_key] and [environment_revision_digest] identify the exact environment configuration
  + [endpoint_key] and [endpoint_revision_digest] identify the exact endpoint configuration
  + [proposed_session_key] and [proposed_session_snapshot_digest] identify the exact proposed binding state
  + [requested_mode] is bind_new, resume_from_predecessor, suspend, release, or expire
  + [proof_refs] remain caller-supplied evidence only
  = must: reject stale or cross-lineage revision and snapshot references
  - never: copy mutable embedded records into a claim and later interpret the copies as current

& [TransitionRecord] makes lifecycle movement explicit
  + [transition_uuid] is immutable identity
  + [subject_key] is one AgentKey or SessionKey
  + [from_snapshot_digest] is absent only for initial formation
  + [to_snapshot_digest] is the exact new immutable snapshot
  + [transition_kind] is one closed transition allowed by the base source
  + [causation_ref] identifies the accepted request or prior event
  + [authority_ref] identifies the authority used for admission
  + [proof_refs] identify validation evidence without proving physical effect
  = must: validate predecessor, exact sequence, subject continuity, transition kind, and authority containment atomically

& [UnchangedBoundary] preserves the base intention
  + candidate profile and CEA1-001 through CEA1-014 identifiers remain unchanged
  + agent continuity remains independent of provider, process, host, model, and embodiment
  + shared immutable Cantor generations and isolated per-agent and per-session state remain required
  + ClaimOnly remains distinct from admission, physical binding, endpoint availability, exclusive ownership, and effect capability
  + resume still creates a new predecessor-linked session
  + all Minecraft-specific types, environment I/O, model calls, storage, clock, adapter, registry, episode, learning, population, and effect work remain excluded

& [CorrectionGovernance] is fail closed
  + the base source remains immutable and visible as historical input
  + later derived artifacts must bind both source snapshots and the identity-state collision fault
  + no explosion or satisfaction signature may treat the base source's combined identity records as canonical
  + [SJS_status] is unprocessed_revision
  + [implementation_authority] is absent
  + [execution_authority] is absent
  + [environment_effect_authority] is absent
  - never: silently edit the base source

